CONFIGURE_COMPONENTS globs components/* and components/test/* and adds every
directory it finds, so the test-only components are built even when the build
is configured with -DWITH_UNIT_TESTS=OFF. Most of that is translation units
compiled and then discarded, but two of the six also install a binary:
mysql_test_event_tracking and mysql_keyring_encryption_test, neither of which a
server installation has any use for. Neither is claimed by a mysql_select slot,
so dropping them does not disturb `port select`.

For 9.x there is a second reason: test_mysql_file_service uses std::filesystem,
which Apple marks as macOS 10.15 or newer, so below that a test component ends
a build that has no other reason to fail.

Follow WITH_UNIT_TESTS. Note that components/test has to be dropped from the
first glob as well as the second: components/* matches the directory itself,
whose CMakeLists.txt declares the components, while components/test/* matches
the subdirectories beneath it. Only that one directory is dropped: components/
example and components/test_server_telemetry_* declare test components of their
own and are left alone, so some component_test_* plugins are still built.

--- a/cmake/component.cmake
+++ b/cmake/component.cmake
@@ -146,7 +146,12 @@
 # Add all CMake projects under components
 MACRO(CONFIGURE_COMPONENTS)
   FILE(GLOB dirs_components ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/components/*)
-  FILE(GLOB dirs_components_test ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/components/test/*)
+  IF(WITH_UNIT_TESTS)
+    FILE(GLOB dirs_components_test ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/components/test/*)
+  ELSE()
+    LIST(REMOVE_ITEM dirs_components ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/components/test)
+    SET(dirs_components_test)
+  ENDIF()
   FOREACH(dir ${dirs_components} ${dirs_components_test})
     IF (EXISTS ${dir}/CMakeLists.txt)
       ADD_SUBDIRECTORY(${dir})
